//
// Usage:
//   Static text:      <span data-i18n="nav.home">Home</span>
//   Placeholder text:  <input data-i18n-placeholder="files.folder_name_ph">
//   Title/tooltip:     <button data-i18n-title="files.rename">
//   From JS:           t('fonts.deleting', {name: family})
//
// Coverage note: this covers the shared chrome (nav/footer), Home, Fonts,
// Settings' own static UI (buttons/messages/Wi-Fi/OPDS sections), and
// File Manager's static UI plus its main user-facing alerts. Two things are
// intentionally NOT covered here, since they need a different approach:
//   1. Settings' individual setting names/categories/option labels — those
//      come from the device's /api/settings JSON (defined in C++), not from
//      this file. Translating them means either localizing that C++ source
//      or building a key-by-key client-side override map once every
//      setting's exact key is known.
//   2. files.js's internal "Conversion Log" technical output (parser/codec
//      diagnostic lines) — left in English as debug output, not
//      user-facing UI chrome.
